  "department": "Fundraising",
  "descriptionHtml": "<h3>About the work from home job/internship</h3><p>She Can Foundation works for the empowerment of women and girls through education, skill development, and livelihood support. This internship is an opportunity to contribute to that mission by supporting the foundation's fundraising efforts.<br>
<br>
Selected intern's day-to-day responsibilities include:<br>
<br>
1. Reaching out to individuals and communities and encouraging them to contribute to the foundation's cause.<br>
2. Sharing the foundation's fundraising campaigns across WhatsApp and social media platforms.<br>
3. Liaising with the foundation team to receive campaign material and share updates with donors.<br>
<br>
On successful completion of the internship, interns will receive a certificate of completion and a letter of recommendation from the foundation. Guidance and support will be provided by the foundation team throughout the internship.<br>
<br>
Performance-based stipend: 20% of the total funds raised.</p>
<h3>Skill(s) required</h3><ul><li>Advanced Excel</li><li>Client Relationship</li><li>Cold Calling</li><li>Community Management</li><li>Content Writing</li><li>Effective Communication</li><li>Email Marketing</li><li>English Proficiency (Spoken)</li><li>English Proficiency (Written)</li><li>Lead Generation</li><li>Marketing Campaigns</li><li>MS-Excel</li><li>Networking</li><li>Problem Solving</li><li>Research and Analytics</li><li>Sales</li><li>Social Media Marketing</li><li>Storytelling</li><li>Strategy</li><li>Time Management</li></ul>
<h3>Who can apply</h3><p>Only those candidates can apply who:</p><ol><li>are available for the work from home job/internship</li><li>can start the work from home job/internship between 25th Nov'26 and 30th Dec'26</li><li>are available for duration of 1 month</li><li>have relevant skills and interests</li><li>Women wanting to start/restart their career can also apply.</li></ol>
<h3>Perks</h3><ul><li>Certificate</li><li>Letter of recommendation</li><li>Flexible work hours</li></ul>
<h3>Additional information</h3><ol><li>Stipend Structure:</li><li>Incentive pay: ₹ 1,500 - 15,000 lump sum</li></ol>
<h3>Number of openings</h3><p>40</p>
<h3>About She Can Foundation</h3><p>The She Can Foundation is an NGO, registered under the Indian Societies Registration Act of 1860, dedicated to uplifting and empowering underprivileged women. Our mission is to provide education, training, and resources to help women from marginalized communities overcome obstacles and achieve their full potential. We work to promote gender equality, increase access to healthcare and education, and provide opportunities for economic growth and development. Through our programs and initiatives, we strive to create a world where every woman has the resources and support she needs to thrive and succeed. Join us in our mission to empower women and help build a brighter future for all.</p>
<h3>Details</h3><ul><li><strong>Start date:</strong> Immediately</li><li><strong>Duration:</strong> 1 Month</li><li><strong>Stipend:</strong> ₹ 1,500 - 15,000 lump sum</li><li><strong>Apply by:</strong> 25 Dec' 26</li></ul>",
