  "companyLogoUrl": "https://internshala-uploads.internshala.com/logo%2F636b3135e04541667969333.png.webp",
  "department": "Human Resources (HR)",
  "descriptionHtml": "<h3>About the work from home job/internship</h3><p>As an HR intern at NayePankh Foundation, you will have the opportunity to immerse yourself in the world of non-profit organizations while gaining hands-on experience in human resources. You will work closely with our HR team to support various initiatives and projects aimed at recruiting, developing, and retaining top talent for our organization. <br>
<br>
Selected intern's day-to-day responsibilities include:<br>
<br>
1. Assist with recruitment efforts by posting job listings, screening resumes, and scheduling interviews.<br>
2. Help onboard new employees by preparing paperwork, coordinating orientation sessions, and ensuring a smooth integration into the company.<br>
3. Support training and development programs by organizing training sessions, tracking employee progress, and collecting feedback.<br>
4. Assist with performance management processes by maintaining employee records, conducting performance evaluations, and addressing any performance-related issues.<br>
5. Contribute to employee engagement initiatives by organizing team-building activities, gathering employee feedback, and implementing programs to enhance the overall employee experience.<br>
6. Assist with benefits administration by enrolling employees in benefit programs, answering benefits-related questions, and ensuring compliance with regulations.<br>
7. Support the HR team with various administrative tasks, such as maintaining HR databases, preparing reports, and ensuring accurate record-keeping. <br>
<br>
If you are a motivated and enthusiastic individual with a passion for HR and making a difference in the community, we invite you to join our team and help us create positive change through our work at NayePankh Foundation.</p>
<h3>Skill(s) required</h3><ul><li>Effective Communication</li><li>English Proficiency (Spoken)</li><li>English Proficiency (Written)</li><li>MS-Excel</li><li>MS-Office</li><li>MS-Word</li></ul>
<h3>Who can apply</h3><p>Only those candidates can apply who:</p><ol><li>are available for the work from home job/internship</li><li>can start the work from home job/internship between 25th Nov'26 and 30th Dec'26</li><li>are available for duration of 1 month</li><li>have relevant skills and interests</li><li>Women wanting to start/restart their career can also apply.</li></ol>
